'docs.overview':'Overview','docs.inbox_mgmt':'Inbox Management','docs.block_mgmt':'Block Management','docs.provider_mgmt':'Provider Management','docs.outlook_pool':'Outlook Account Pool','docs.yyds_pool':'YYDS Mail Pool','docs.imap_pool':'IMAP Domain Mail','docs.icloud_pool':'iCloud Aliases','docs.nav_ic_list':'List Apple IDs','docs.nav_ic_add':'Add Apple ID','docs.nav_ic_test':'Test both halves','docs.nav_ic_cookies':'Replace cookie','docs.nav_ic_srp':'SRP sign-in','docs.nav_ic_generate':'Mint addresses','docs.nav_ic_addresses':'Address pool','docs.nav_ic_mail':'Read by address','docs.nav_ic_retire':'Retire address','docs.ic_intro':'Hide My Email is a forwarding alias, not a mailbox: Apple exposes no API for reading mail sent to one. So this provider has two halves — minting goes through Apple private endpoints, reading goes through IMAP on whichever mailbox the aliases forward to. That mailbox is frequently not an Apple one; an Apple ID registered with a Gmail address needs imap.gmail.com. Requires iCloud+. An Apple ID is capped at 750 addresses for its lifetime, so addresses are recycled rather than minted per inbox.','docs.ic_list_desc':'List every Apple ID','docs.ic_status_note':'Three states: active means both halves work; degraded means the session expired — existing addresses still receive, but none can be minted; error means reading is broken and dispatch skips the account. Cookies, the Apple ID password, the trust token and the IMAP password are never returned.','docs.ic_add_desc':'Add an Apple ID','docs.ic_add_note':'cookies takes whatever the browser gave you: Copy as cURL in any shell, Copy as PowerShell, a cookie extension JSON export, or a bare Cookie header. A paste missing X-APPLE-WEBAUTH-TOKEN or X-APPLE-WEBAUTH-USER is refused with 400 naming the missing one, rather than stored to fail later.','docs.ic_test_desc':'Check the minting and reading halves together','docs.ic_test_note':'The two errors come back separately because they are fixed in different places: the cookie at icloud.com, the IMAP password at whichever provider hosts the receiving mailbox. forwardTo is where Hide My Email actually delivers, and forwardMismatch says so outright when it differs from the IMAP login.','docs.ic_cookies_desc':'Swap an expired cookie in place','docs.ic_cookies_note':'Keeps the address pool. Deleting and recreating the account would burn every alias it holds — each one occupies a slot out of 750.','docs.ic_srp_desc':'Sign in over SRP so a trust token replaces the cookie','docs.ic_srp_then':'Then','docs.ic_srp_note':'A cookie expires within hours; a trust token lasts far longer, so the six-digit code is entered once per Apple ID rather than once per session. When Apple accepts a stored trust token, needsMfa is false and no code is sent at all. Sessions expire after five minutes; the in-flight handshake lives in memory, so a restart loses it and you sign in again. With no Apple device to hand, use phones + sms.','docs.ic_generate_desc':'Mint addresses now (manual top-up)','docs.ic_generate_note':'The scheduled task is the normal path; this is for emergencies. Apple refusals come back in its own wording — its error taxonomy is undocumented, so none is invented. The auto-refill switch and target live on the iCloud page, or under PATCH /api/admin/settings as icloud_pool_enabled / icloud_pool_target (clamped at 750).','docs.ic_addresses_desc':'The address pool','docs.ic_addresses_note':'Three states: free is in the pool and claimable; assigned is held by a live inbox; retired was deactivated at Apple and is never handed out again, with its slot spent for good.','docs.ic_mail_desc':'Read an address\u2019s mail (plus /:uid detail)','docs.ic_mail_note':'Everything that ever arrived at the address, unlike /api/inbox/:id/messages which hides anything older than the inbox asking. Answers "has this address ever received anything".','docs.ic_retire_desc':'Retire a burned address','docs.ic_retire_note':'Stops forwarding at Apple and never hands it out again. Returns 409 while an inbox holds it. The slot it occupies never comes back — 750 is the lifetime total for one Apple ID.','docs.key_mgmt':'API Key Management','docs.ai_integration':'AI / LLM Integration',
